le i  also want to note that whitney has often  said that she is not gluten and  dairy-free because it's healthier but  because removing these from her diet has  helped her better manage her psoriasis  now we've briefly discussed psoriasis in  my downshiftology video right here but  in short we know that autoimmune  disorders like this often compromise gut  integrity making it more difficult to  tolerate a lot of different foods we  also often see that autoimmune disorders  tend to overlap so folks with psoriasis  are more likely to also have celiac  disease which would absolutely warrant a  gluten-free diet however there's no  standard diet protocol for psoriasis and  the evidence for eliminating gluten in  dairy is mixed and inconclusive probably  because it is highly individualized so  it's important to work with a dietitian  to tease out your unique food triggers  so that you can keep the widest variety  of foods possible in your diet while  still feeling good it's also just as  important to focus on foods that we can  add to help support the gut and reduce  the inflammatory response like omega-3  fats vitamin d selenium probiotics and  antioxidant rich foods taken i'm taking  a break from powdered pre-workout but if  i ever need like a little bit of energy  before my workout or in the middle of my  workout like a little mid-afternoon  pick-me-up but it's a mid-workout  picking me up i'll just sip on my  laundry new energy drink and i brought  my water out here  one drinks for fun  one drinks for hydration if you love  energy drinks to boost performance  during a workout fine i really don't  care how you get your caffeine but keep  in mind that drinks like the iolani new  energy drink contains around 200  milligrams of caffeine which is  equivalent to two cups of your usual  drip coffee or more than three shots of  espresso  so if you're sensitive to caffeine you  may want to be mindful of other sources  in the day  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  now that's how you 