 is why mechanical eating will  often be recommended in cases like this  so this would mean having set meal times  every day to ensure that you are getting  regular calories and nutrition in your  system as your body starts to  re-regulate even if your appetite  doesn't really agree with you at that  time and this is especially important  because a lack of calories and nutrition  can actually further exacerbate  depressive symptoms and negatively  impact energy levels which kind of  creates a bit of a vicious cycle it's  often important to have a handful of  super easy convenient meals on hand that  can be warmed up or whipped up really  quickly without thinking about it on  overwhelming days so whitney's protein  smoothie from earlier is a perfect  example of this as most folks with  really poor appetite will find that  drinking their calories are a lot easier  for them than eating them now i share  more tips on how to bump up the calories  and nutrition of food in my weight gain  video right here which can definitely be  applied in these cases as well lastly  well ultimately the goal for a lot of  folks with depression is just to eat  anything at all for days where we do  have a little bit more motivation  focusing on foods rich in omega-3 fats b  vitamins and protein may help to support  our mood-boosting neurotransmitters in  the brain  love this quick little hunger crushing  combo so we're getting some protein and  healthy fats from the peanut butter and  some fiber in the blueberries this would  be a really great easy snack idea for  days that you just like can't think  about meal prep  no let's finish off with dinner  [Music]  for a simple meal i gotta say like a  pecan crusted chicken it's quite  elevated in my books i mean it's a step  up from what i do on on really lazy  nights but nut crusting a lean protein  like chicken is a great way to boost  those calories and add some healthy fats  without too much fuss we've got protein  from the chicken fiber from the sweet  potatoes and green beans as well as some  healthy fats from the pecans so another  solid balanced meal that looks insanely  delish  delicious but on days when the energy  and motivation to cook is lower you  could easily swap in a little chopped up  rotisserie chicken throw a little salad  kit together on the side and then like  microwave some minute rice for some  carbs healthy balanced eating doesn't  have to be complicated so what are my  overall thoughts on whitney's diet based  on our calculations on this particular  day winnie's consuming a solid amount of  calories which i think are in line with  her needs a lot of people might be  thinking like oh wow that's a lot of  food but whitney is a very active young  woman with a solid amount of muscle mass  and that muscle mass is going to  upregulate our metabolism to support it  it's also not uncommon for folks who go  through depressive episodes and a low  appetite as a result of that to see  their body kind of play catch up when  they're feeling a little bit better so  that they can see larger than average  fluctuations in their daily caloric  needs but i do get the sense from  watching whitney often that she has a  generally healthy balanced relationship  with food with a focus on variety easy  meals and ultimately self-care and i  think that winnie is a perfect example  of how food and movement can be used as  a means for self-care rather than  self-control and how to treat yourself  and your body with kindness and  nourishment when times are tough so on  that note that's all that i have for you  guys today thank you again to obey for  sponsoring if you like this video be  sure to give it the thumbs up leave me a  comment below on who or what you'd like  senior review next subscribe to the  channel and i'll see you next time on  abby's kitchen bye  [Music]
 

